docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:20:- **Manual-fetch (MFK/MR/PCMF) ingest.** The 335 hand-curated PDFs in `raw/Manual Fetch Kimi /`, `raw/Manual Resourcing/`, `raw/Papers Cube Manual Fetch/`. Runs via the autonomy daemon (`tools/autonomy/daemon-tick.sh` → `tools/autonomy/ingest-manual-fetch-batch.mjs`). Every 30 minutes, picks up to 2 unprocessed PDFs, runs the full Cochrane workflow (read PDF + identity-check + write fresh OR merge-enhance + spawn fresh-context audit subagent + apply audit findings + commit). Per-PDF state tracked at `data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv`.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:46:- **Convergence point with daemon:** daemon is still loaded in launchd and ticking. The per-PDF tracker (`data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv`) prevents race conditions — either agent that claims a PDF first wins; the other skips. Daemon will simply exit cleanly each tick after finding nothing un-tracked in its priority order, which is fine. **Papers Cube Manual Fetch is now FULLY done as of 2026-05-18 (Claude completed the rotation); Children Personal Care Papers is also fully done.** No active claim conflicts with Claude Code; both those folders should be skipped.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:130:2. **DRAIN-FOLDER goal**: every PDF in a named folder ends the session either represented by a `wiki/sources/*.md` page (real ingest), folded into an existing source page (same-DOI rollup), or marked in `data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv` with an explicit `skip:*` / `fail:*` / `ingested` decision. Folder ends empty of un-dispositioned PDFs.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:144:4. **TRIAGE-FIRST FOR DRAIN-FOLDER GOALS.** Auto-fetched wishlist folders are heavily padded with same-DOI duplicates, false-positives, and download failures. The drain-folder goal is met fastest by: (a) opening every PDF in the folder in parallel batches of 10, (b) classifying each as `real-ingest` / `dedup-rollup` / `skip:<reason>` / `blocker`, (c) batch-committing all `dedup-rollup` and `skip:*` decisions to `wishlist-fetch-audit.csv` in one or two commits, (d) then doing real ingests on the remaining `real-ingest` pile. Interleaving triage with full ingest per PDF is slower.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:161:- ❌ "Agent tool / sub-task spawn failed" — best-effort audit policy (locked 2026-05-18). Commit the page with `status=pending-audit-spawn-failed` and CONTINUE.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:169:The full backlog (manual-fetch PDFs + strict-recheck rows + Marker corpus + auto-fetched wishlist accumulations) is NOT a single-session goal. Multiple sessions are expected. Each session's job is to meet its named goal, no more, no less.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:173:- Do NOT ingest manual-fetch PDFs from folders assigned to Claude's daemon (06_Infant_Foods_Formula, Children Personal Care Papers, 04_Meat_Poultry_Seafood, 03_Grains_and_Grain_Products, 05_Dairy_Eggs_and_Alternatives). The daemon owns these. Codex's ingest assignment is the bottom-up priority list (condiments, nuts/seeds, processed, vegetables, fruits, Papers Cube, Manual Resourcing). Before ingesting any PDF, check `data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv` — if the PDF is already tracked, skip it (the daemon claimed it).
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:201:How: parallel-Read 5-10 source pages + their PDFs per tool message, audit each per docs/gpt-collaboration/audit-prompt.md (5 checks; Check 4 strict brand firewall; Exception 2 permits instrument/CRM/software vendor names in Methods). Apply real findings, commit per page, update queue row. If audit spawn fails with thread limit, commit page with status=pending-audit-spawn-failed and continue — never stop on spawn failure.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:208:### Template B — DRAIN-FOLDER (auto-fetched wishlist or manual-fetch)
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:211:GOAL: <FOLDER_PATH> has 0 un-dispositioned PDFs. Every PDF ends either represented by a wiki/sources/*.md page (real ingest), folded into an existing page as a same-DOI rollup (with the wishlist row marked ingested), or marked in data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv with an explicit skip:<reason> or fail:<reason> decision. Stop when met OR hard blocker (paper-internal contradiction, DOI conflict).
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:213:How: TRIAGE FIRST. Open every PDF in the folder in parallel batches of 10. Classify each as (a) real-ingest, (b) dedup-rollup, (c) skip:<reason>, (d) blocker. Batch-commit all (b)+(c) decisions to wishlist-fetch-audit.csv in one or two commits. Then real-ingest the (a) pile, batch-committing every ~10 source pages. Per CLAUDE.md Part 4, do NOT commit per-paper.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:215:Audit each new source page per audit-prompt.md (best-effort: commit with status=pending-audit-spawn-failed if spawn errors, do not stop). Routing audit (`npm run evidence:source-routes`) runs ONCE at session end. Frontmatter discipline per CLAUDE.md Part 5 — products/ingredients/matrices/metals/jurisdictions at the level of specificity the source states.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:12:GOAL: drain raw/manual-fetch/seasonal-geographic-variance/auto-fetched/ to 0 PDFs. The wishlist fetcher in the daemon is producing 100–250 PDFs/hour into this folder. You are the primary consumer alongside the Claude/Opus daemon, which picks up residuals at a hard per-tick cap of 3 PDFs as of 2026-05-28 (see tools/autonomy/ingest-manual-fetch-batch.mjs). Stop only when the folder is empty OR a named hard blocker fires (see ESCALATION below). No time budget. No "feels enough." No self-invented stop criteria. The earlier "drain to ≤10" threshold (pre-2026-05-28) left residuals stuck indefinitely: Codex would no-op on every fire whenever the queue dropped below 10, while the daemon also skipped this folder. Both ends now drain to zero.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:15:  ls raw/manual-fetch/seasonal-geographic-variance/auto-fetched/*.pdf > /tmp/codex-snapshot-$(date +%s).txt
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:19:STEP 2 — RACE-SAFE CLAIM. Before processing any PDF, check data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv. If a row matches the PDF's filename AND status starts with "claimed" or "ingested", SKIP it (daemon may be mid-process). Otherwise add a row with status="claimed-by-codex" + a timestamp before touching the PDF. This prevents double-ingest races.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:24:  (c) skip:<reason> — false positive. Use existing vocabulary in data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv (skip:no-heavy-metal-data / skip:not-target-cell / skip:not-food-occurrence / skip:review-only-no-primary-data / skip:not-pdf:<content-type>)
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:27:Batch-commit ALL (b)+(c) decisions to data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv in ONE commit titled:
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:48:  ingest auto-fetched <date> <time> batch N: K source pages
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:53:STEP 5 — UPDATE TRACKER. After each source page is committed, update its row in data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv to status="ingested-by-codex" with the commit hash.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:55:STEP 6 — AUDIT (best-effort). After each batch, try to spawn fresh-context audits per docs/gpt-collaboration/audit-prompt.md (5 checks: numerical fidelity, slug vocabulary, speciation/methods, brand firewall, wiki/HMTc firewall). If `agent thread limit reached`, write each page's audit-queue row with status=pending-audit-spawn-failed and CONTINUE. NEVER stop on spawn failure — Claude drains the async-audit lane separately.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:58:  node tools/autonomy/auto-fetched-hygiene.mjs --report
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:91:  - audit-queue rows added with status=pending-audit-spawn-failed
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:93:  - final auto-fetched/ depth
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:103:**Race safety with the daemon.** The daemon ingests from `raw/Manual Fetch Kimi/`, `raw/Papers Cube Manual Fetch/`, `raw/Manual Resourcing/`, and `raw/Manual Fetch Discovery/`. Codex ingests from `raw/manual-fetch/seasonal-geographic-variance/auto-fetched/`. Different folders → no overlap → no race. The tracker check is a belt-and-suspenders safety for the case where someone (Codex or the daemon) gets pointed at the wrong folder by accident.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:117:- auto-fetched/ depth fluctuating (refill→drain→refill, not stuck)
