have shown that ZON can be found in the range of 0.001 and
175 mg/kg in cereals for human consumption. It is important
to investigate the presence of ZON and its metabolites in
commercial cereal-based infant formulas analysed with the
developed method since the long-term effects of endocrine
disrupting effects, especially with chronic exposure, cannot
be predicted in infants, who are in the most sensitive period
and open to all kinds of negative effects.
