milk samples used in validation studies. Cathelicidin has also
been identiﬁed as a biomarker in Streptococcus agalactiae
caused cases of mastitis, although by use of the classic proteomic method of two-dimensional electrophoresis along
with MS (Pongthaisong et al., 2016).
