for HMs analysis through an atomic absorption spectrophotometer. The analysis was performed in triplicate
for quality ­assurance45.

Human health risk assessment of HMs via consumption of fish

Different methods have been used for the determination of the risk associated with the consumption of
contaminated fish. Estimated daily intake is one of the most common methods to help identify the number
of pollutants consumed daily. For determining health risk related to HM via the consumption of fish were
determined by using the following ­indices46,47.

Estimated daily intake of HMs (EDI)

Daily intake of HMs via consumption of fish was determined by using the following equation:

EDI =

CM × FIR
