Health risk due to the eating of contaminated fish with metal was determined by using HRI. The value of HRI
less than 1 is said to be safe for the exposed population. Where HRI above 1 means that there is a chance of noncarcinogenic effect on the exposed population. To determine HRI, the following equation was ­used49.

