Perfluoroalkyl substances (PFASs) are a complex group of
man-made chemicals with a chemical structure consisting
of a perfluorinated carbon tail (hydrophobic/lipophobic end)
and an anionic head group (hydrophilic end). Beginning in
the middle of the last century, they are used for several industrial applications including the production of water repellent
clothes or cookware. The compounds have a high stability
and mobility, and after release from industrial sources and
everyday objects, these properties have led to ubiquitous
