We also identified 14 OTUs that were negatively associated with natural log-transformed infant urinary arsenic concentration, among them, OTUs assigned to the family Clostridiaceae and to the genera Bacteroides and
Bifidobacterium. Overall, positively associated OTUs were largely from the phylum Firmicutes, while the majority
of negatively associated OTUs were from the phyla Firmicutes or Bacteroidetes. Different OTUs representing
bacteria of the genera Lactobacillus and Dorea were found to be both positively and negatively associated with
natural log-transformed urinary arsenic concentration.

