+# Oviri et al. 2024 - Heavy metals in bathing soaps in Nigeria
+
+This Nigerian bathing-soap survey measured Pb, Ni, Zn, Co, Cd, and Cr in 17 soap samples across medicated, moisturizing, toilet, and skin-whitening categories. Whole-study ranges were Pb 0.08-0.39 mg/kg, Ni 0.05-0.33 mg/kg, Zn 0.10-6.42 mg/kg, Co 0.04-1.93 mg/kg, Cd 0.02-0.09 mg/kg, and Cr 0.01-0.19 mg/kg. The source is routeable to bathing soap and skin-whitening personal-care evidence surfaces.
+
+## Key numbers
+
+Table 3 reports category summaries in mg/kg:
+
+| Soap class | Pb mean +/- SD (range) | Ni mean +/- SD (range) | Zn mean +/- SD (range) |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| Medicated | 0.108 +/- 0.031 (0.08-0.16) | 0.176 +/- 0.04 (0.12-0.22) | 0.488 +/- 0.348 (0.18-1.03) |
+| Moisturizing | 0.135 +/- 0.040 (0.10-0.21) | 0.204 +/- 0.073 (0.05-0.24) | 1.660 +/- 2.434 (0.10-6.42) |
+| Toilet | 0.200 +/- 0.072 (0.14-0.28) | 0.177 +/- 0.042 (0.13-0.21) | 0.530 +/- 0.106 (0.41-0.61) |
+| Skin whitening | 0.170 +/- 0.046 (0.12-0.21) | 0.143 +/- 0.058 (0.11-0.21) | 0.410 +/- 0.173 (0.30-0.61) |
+
+| Soap class | Co mean +/- SD (range) | Cd mean +/- SD (range) | Cr mean +/- SD (range) |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| Medicated | 0.836 +/- 0.645 (0.33-1.93) | 0.032 +/- 0.011 (0.02-0.05) | 0.048 +/- 0.02 (0.03-0.07) |
+| Moisturizing | 0.794 +/- 0.175 (0.59-1.01) | 0.042 +/- 0.010 (0.02-0.05) | 0.028 +/- 0.023 (0.01-0.07) |
+| Toilet | 0.730 +/- 0.070 (0.66-0.80) | 0.047 +/- 0.006 (0.04-0.05) | 0.077 +/- 0.012 (0.07-0.09) |
+| Skin whitening | 0.507 +/- 0.195 (0.42 not shown as range low in OCR; source table range begins 0.30 class text for Zn and 0.03-0.07 for Cd/Cr context) | 0.033 +/- 0.015 (0.03 median) | 0.060 +/- 0.017 (0.07 median) |
+
+## Methods (brief)
+
+Soap samples were digested with nitric acid and analyzed using flame atomic absorption spectrophotometry. The paper also estimates dermal exposure and non-carcinogenic/carcinogenic risk parameters.
+
+## Implications
+
+Bathing soaps and skin-whitening soaps in this Nigerian sample set contain measurable Pb, Cd, Cr, Ni, Co, and Zn. The source supports finished-product personal-care occurrence evidence and should not be treated as an ingredient-only study.
+
