+# Afridi et al. 2023 - Lead in lipstick, face powder, eye liner, and eye shadow from Pakistan
+
+This paper combines Pb measurements in cosmetics with dermatitis-patient biomonitoring. The routeable product occurrence portion covers lipstick, face powder, eye liner, and eye shadow samples from Pakistan, with product-class Pb ranges reported in ug/g. The biomarker results are health-context evidence and should not be routed as product concentrations.
+
+## Key numbers
+
+The abstract reports product-class Pb ranges in ug/g:
+
+| Product class | Sample count | Pb range |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Lipstick | 15 | 50.5-120 |
+| Face powder | 13 | 14.6-30.7 |
+| Eye liner | 11 | 2.87-4.25 |
+| Eye shadow | 15 | 15.3-21.6 |
+
+Table 5 gives individual product values and confirms Pb in all listed cosmetic classes. The public page preserves product-class ranges rather than consumer brand names.
+
+## Methods (brief)
+
+Cosmetic products were digested with nitric acid and hydrogen peroxide using microwave-assisted digestion. Pb was measured by electrothermal atomic absorption spectrophotometry, with certified reference materials used to verify the analytical method. Blood and serum samples from dermatitis patients were analyzed separately.
+
+## Implications
+
+The source supports product-class occurrence evidence for Pb in makeup products in the Pakistan market. The high lipstick range is especially relevant for lip-contact cosmetics, while face powder and eye makeup provide additional leave-on exposure context.
